<p>NOTE: During the March 1997 quarter, Delta recorded $52 million in restructuring and other non-recurring charges related to its previously announced realignment of transatlantic operations.</p>
<p>The company announced on January 7, 1997 that it anticipated recording up to $60 million in restructuring and other non-recurring charges in the March quarter related to these changes.  </p>
<p>During the March 1996 quarter, Delta recorded $556 million in restructuring and other non-recurring charges related to the write-down of its Lockheed L-1011 fleet and the continuation of its Leadership 7.5 cost reduction program.</p>
<p>Including restructuring and other non-recurring charges, Delta's fully diluted and primary earnings per common share were $2.52 and $2.47, respectively, in the March 1997 quarter.</p>
<p>This compares to a fully diluted and primary loss per common share of $5.77 in the March 1996 quarter, including restructuring and other non-recurring charges.</p>
<p>Excluding the charges, Delta recorded fully diluted earnings per common share after preferred stock dividend requirements of $2.88, compared with $0.80 in the March 1996 quarter. Primary earnings per common share after preferred stock dividends was $2.95 in the March 1997 quarter compared with $0.80 in the March 1996 quarter. Meanwhile, operating revenue for the March 1997 quarter increased 15 percent to $3.4 billion from $3.0 billion in the March 1996 quarter.</p>
